#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sbxfs — in-sandbox filesystem CLI (stdlib only, + ripgrep for grep).

File work runs inside the sandbox and returns structured JSON, so the host never
pulls whole files across the boundary to loop over them. Invoked as:

    sbxfs <op> '<json-params>'

ops: read, write, edit, grep, glob. Output is a single JSON object on stdout — the
result on success, or {"error": "..."} (exit 1) on a handled failure. grep shells out
to `rg --json` when ripgrep is on PATH and falls back to a stdlib walk with identical
semantics otherwise; a .pdf read shells out to poppler-utils (pdfinfo/pdftotext/pdftoppm)
to return extracted text plus page images, degrading to text-only when poppler is absent;
a .pptx read converts to pdf with libreoffice (soffice) and reuses that path so slides come
back as images; everything else is pure stdlib.
"""

